      "description": "SteelFlow turns dimensions into a clear, verifiable metal estimate—and turns that estimate into a client-ready quote.\n\nCALCULATE METAL WEIGHT\n\nChoose a profile, enter dimensions and quantity, and see unit weight, total weight, surface area, volume, and the formula behind the result. SteelFlow supports common profiles including plate and flat bar, round, square, hexagonal and octagonal bar, round, square and rectangular tube, angle, channel, I/H sections, T sections, and custom cross-sectional area.\n\nESTIMATE REAL PROJECT COST\n\nPrice material by kg, lb, meter, foot, or piece. Add waste, processing charges, transport or other fixed fees, markup or margin, and tax. Currency-aware rounding keeps totals practical for real quotes.\n\nBUILD PROJECTS, NOT LOOSE CALCULATIONS\n\nSave multiple material items into a project, duplicate and reorder them, update pricing, and keep every dimension and assumption traceable. See total quantity, weight, material cost, fees, tax, and quote total in one place.\n\nSHARE PROFESSIONAL OUTPUT\n\nCreate a polished PDF quote or export a machine-friendly CSV material list. Add company and customer details, terms, validity, and notes before sharing.\n\nMATERIALS AND UNITS THAT FIT YOUR WORK\n\nUse built-in densities for carbon steel, stainless steel, aluminum, copper, brass, titanium and more, or create custom materials. Work in metric or imperial units without rebuilding a calculation.\n\nPRIVATE AND OFFLINE\n\nNo account is required. Project and material data stays on your device by default, core calculations work offline, and versioned local backup helps you move or restore your records.\n\nFREE TO START, ONE-TIME PRO UPGRADE\n\nQuick calculations and essential project tools are free. SteelFlow Pro unlocks unlimited projects and items, custom materials, company details and quote terms, CSV export, unbranded PDF quotes, versioned backup, and bulk pricing with one non-consumable purchase—no subscription.\n\nIMPORTANT\n\nWeights and prices are theoretical estimates based on your inputs, reference densities, and common engineering formulas. Verify material grades, current standards, supplier data, drawings, and actual stock before purchasing, fabrication, transport planning, structural design, settlement, or contract use.",
